1
00:01:58,804 --> 00:02:01,224
What's the highest fall
anyone has ever survived

2
00:02:01,224 --> 00:02:02,164
without a parachute?

3
00:02:02,924 --> 00:02:06,524
According to Guinness
World Records, it's 10,160

4
00:02:06,524 --> 00:02:08,004
metres.

5
00:02:08,924 --> 00:02:12,644
In January 1972, a Yugoslav
airliner broke apart

6
00:02:12,644 --> 00:02:15,104
in the sky over what
was then Czechoslovakia.

7
00:02:15,884 --> 00:02:17,904
The official investigation
blamed a bomb.

8
00:02:18,704 --> 00:02:21,144
Twenty-eight people were
on board, and twenty-seven

9
00:02:21,144 --> 00:02:21,944
of them died.

10
00:02:22,564 --> 00:02:25,044
The one survivor was a
22-year-old flight attendant

11
00:02:25,044 --> 00:02:26,384
called Vesna Vulović.

12
00:02:27,324 --> 00:02:29,524
A man from a nearby village
found her trapped in

13
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:31,164
the wreckage, badly injured.

14
00:02:31,884 --> 00:02:34,404
She was in a coma for
three days, and it took her

15
00:02:34,404 --> 00:02:35,404
months to walk again.

16
00:02:36,104 --> 00:02:36,904
But she lived.

17
00:02:37,484 --> 00:02:39,644
And her fall, from the
plane's cruising height,

18
00:02:40,004 --> 00:02:41,204
went into the record books.

19
00:02:42,004 --> 00:02:46,344
Then, in 2009, two journalists
challenged that number.

20
00:02:47,064 --> 00:02:49,564
They argued the plane
actually broke up much lower,

21
00:02:50,104 --> 00:02:53,064
maybe only a few hundred
metres up, after a fast

22
00:02:53,064 --> 00:02:54,024
emergency descent.

23
00:02:54,804 --> 00:02:57,044
They pointed to how small an
area the wreckage covered,

24
00:02:57,544 --> 00:02:59,604
and to people on the ground
who saw it come down.

25
00:03:00,384 --> 00:03:02,244
They even suggested the
plane might have been shot

26
00:03:02,244 --> 00:03:04,824
down by mistake, and that
the high-altitude bomb

27
00:03:04,824 --> 00:03:06,604
story was invented to hide it.

28
00:03:07,044 --> 00:03:08,824
But one of the journalists
admitted the evidence

29
00:03:08,824 --> 00:03:11,964
was only circumstantial, and
it has never been proved.

30
00:03:12,544 --> 00:03:13,884
Guinness still lists the record.

31
00:03:14,684 --> 00:03:17,764
So was it 10 kilometres,
or a few hundred metres?

32
00:03:18,664 --> 00:03:21,204
Either way, she survived
something almost nobody

33
00:03:21,204 --> 00:03:22,004
survives.

34
00:03:22,684 --> 00:03:24,844
We just may never know
how far she really fell.
